---
description: |
  Detects the SOC Prime High-Order Sigma rule "The n8n n8mare How threat
  actors are misusing AI workflow automation".

  The n8n n8mare How threat actors are misusing AI workflow automation

  The rule chains 5 stages of SOC Prime behavior rules by host. See
  `socprime::hos::chain` for the correlation and the resulting Detection
  Finding.
args:
  named:
    - name: timeframe
      type: duration
      default: 5min
      description: The time span that a chain must fit into.
    - name: threshold
      type: float
      default: 0.6
      description: The share of stages a host must cover, between 0 and 1.
    - name: tolerance
      type: duration
      default: 1min
      description: How far findings of a host may arrive out of time order.
---

// Generated by scripts/vendor.py from the SOC Prime HoS rule UfhULfdvVPtu.
let $stages = {
  seq1: [
    "df03915e-4d53-4fad-94f2-8310906315f9", // Suspicious Executions from User Default Folders v2 (via process_creation)
  ],
  seq2: [
    "309111d8-89ad-4c98-a799-10053a40bd0a", // Suspicious Powershell Strings (via powershell)
    "cfdbe1fa-ff01-44a4-b8e4-782c86099768", // Suspicious Powershell Strings (via cmdline)
    "c77d19cf-3624-4e67-9474-69b44568d39f", // Powershell Executing File In Suspicious Directory Using Bypass Execution Policy (via cmdline)
    "7c01d1e4-89de-476f-a996-eb768978994a", // The Possibility of Execution Through Hidden PowerShell Command Lines (via cmdline)
  ],
  seq3: [
    "68c59aa9-2052-4971-8962-667a45fb6f8c", // Alternative Remote Access / Management Software (via process_creation)
  ],
  seq4: [
    "39fd7f61-89d5-4fe2-8c00-534506d06b10", // Possible Manual Service or Driver Install for Persistence (via cmdline)
  ],
  seq5: [
    "93ec52aa-776a-4976-8209-bc68321c75b7", // Possible Data Exfiltration over WebRequests (via powershell)
    "1f21ec3f-810d-4b0e-8045-322202e22b4b", // Network Connection Initiated By PowerShell Process
  ],
}
sigma rules=[...$stages.seq1, ...$stages.seq2, ...$stages.seq3, ...$stages.seq4, ...$stages.seq5].map(uid => socprime::$rules[uid])
socprime::hos::chain uid="9420e91b-1447-41aa-8cf2-072ec03818d6",
  name="The n8n n8mare How threat actors are misusing AI workflow automation",
  level="high",
  tags=[
    "attack.t1204",
    "attack.t1033",
    "attack.t1564",
    "attack.t1053.005",
    "attack.t1059.001",
    "attack.t1059.005",
    "attack.t1218.005",
    "attack.t1219.002",
    "attack.t1569.002",
    "attack.t1567",
  ],
  stages=$stages,
  timeframe=$timeframe,
  threshold=$threshold,
  tolerance=$tolerance
